// Tesseract Network policy (Headscale v0.29 policy v2, ADR 0014).
// Every account is one Headscale user (u-<accountId>). A device may reach only devices of the same user:
// `autogroup:self` matches nodes owned by the source node's user, and everything else is denied by default.
// Device keys are issued without ACL tags on purpose: since Headscale 0.28 a tagged node is owned by its tags,
// not by a user, so it would fall outside `autogroup:self` (and a shared tag would join every account's devices).
{
  "acls": [
    {
      "action": "accept",
      "src": ["autogroup:member"],
      "dst": ["autogroup:self:*"],
    },
  ],
}
